# Italian closes a mid vowel where Polish leaves it open.
#
# make_ital_phon_adjustments has three arms that put one phoneme in place of
# another. The first turns an n before a k into the velar nasal, which Polish
# wants and which is why bank is bank. The other two close a mid vowel: ɛ
# becomes e and ɔ becomes o, by a context Italian's orthography needs and
# Polish's does not have -- Polish e is ɛ wherever it stands and Polish o is ɔ.
#
# So those two arms now put back the vowel they were given. Doing it that way
# rather than by cutting the arm out keeps the machine's bookkeeping exactly as
# it was: the same insert of the same length happens at the same point, and
# nothing downstream can tell that anything was skipped.
#
# Each is IBM's own wrapper with one symbol changed, written as raw lower
# notation so that nothing else about them can differ from it. Both are bare,
# which is the shape a wrapper has: they stand inside somebody else's rule and
# the choice points around them are that rule's.
#
# This is also what frees the close-mid e for Polish's y. With the letter e
# spoken as ɛ and this arm no longer closing it, nothing produces e but the
# rule for y.

rule pol_keep_open_e takes 1 from glob.obj
  bare
  raw load movl state 0 into r6
  raw load movl state 840 into r0
  raw push state 840
  raw load movl state 832 into r0
  raw push state 832
  raw push state 0
  raw call lpta_rpta_loadp arity 3 depth 3
  raw push imm 0
  raw push sym ZZstring139
  raw push imm 1
  raw push imm 2
  raw push state 0
  raw call insert_2pt_s arity 5 depth 8
  raw popn 8
  raw return reg r0
end

rule pol_keep_open_o takes 1 from glob.obj
  bare
  raw load movl state 0 into r6
  raw load movl state 840 into r0
  raw push state 840
  raw load movl state 832 into r0
  raw push state 832
  raw push state 0
  raw call lpta_rpta_loadp arity 3 depth 3
  raw push imm 0
  raw push sym ZZstring154
  raw push imm 1
  raw push imm 2
  raw push state 0
  raw call insert_2pt_s arity 5 depth 8
  raw popn 8
  raw return reg r0
end
